OpenXR Simulator @PROJECT_VERSION@

This is a development qualification package. Native Windows and the remaining
hardware/application acceptance rows are not yet release-qualified.

Extract the entire archive into a new directory. Keep bin/openxr_simulator.json
beside its runtime library; its relative path allows moving the package.

Launch bin/simxr_companion and create a launch profile with the application's
executable and this package's bin/openxr_simulator.json. Runtime selection affects
that child process only when the OpenXR loader permits environment overrides.
Run Windows applications without elevation: elevated loaders ignore XR_RUNTIME_JSON.
For command-line launch, set XR_RUNTIME_JSON to the absolute manifest path in the
application's environment. This avoids system registration when the loader
permits environment overrides. The tested Proton environment reports elevated
integrity; qualification used runtime registration inside an isolated prefix.
Child-local runtime selection in that environment remains unresolved. On Linux,
bin/launch-linux.py also launches and attaches the companion.

The host needs its graphics driver and Vulkan loader. Linux additionally needs
the usual C/C++ runtime and desktop window-system libraries. This archive does
not install or replace drivers. Windows requires a Vulkan-capable driver even
when the application uses Direct3D or OpenGL.

bin/simxr_companion --version
bin/simxr_runner --version

Python 3.10+ SDK: install share/simxr/sdk/python into a virtual environment with
pip, or put that directory on PYTHONPATH. Examples are in share/simxr/examples;
Luau rigs are also in share/simxr/rigs. The C game bridge header is in include.
See share/doc/simxr for runner and control protocol instructions. Optional loader
probes are in bin when built with SIMXR_BUILD_PROBES.

To uninstall, close this package's processes and delete the extracted directory.
Remove any XR_RUNTIME_JSON setting you added to your own launch scripts. User
settings and recordings are outside the package and are preserved. Extraction
and launch never change the machine's default OpenXR runtime.
